  "about": "Microscope light-path presets (BSD-3-Clause): laser lines, dichroic mirrors and emission filters. 'ideal' entries are defined here (transmission 0/1 with edges); 'fpbase' entries name an FPbase spectrum id whose curve tools/fetch_fpbase.mjs stores in fpbase_spectra.json (CC BY-SA 4.0). Laser intensities are at the sample, kW/cm^2; a dichroic reflects the excitation (R = 1 - T) and transmits the emission (T). presets: named illumination + filter sets; each dye mode in library.json names one (lightPreset), applied when a structure's dye or mode changes (viewer, Micro-Manager) or with light-preset (cli). Intensities with a source cite it; the rest are estimates.",
